  "question": {
    "text": "A cell of emf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> and internal resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is connected in series with an external resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></math>. Then what will be the ratio of the terminal potential difference to emf, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.",
    "image": null
